| **Medium** | Oil on canvas |
| **Dimensions** | 44 ¾ × 34½ in. (113.7 × 87.6 cm) |
| **Primary image URL** | https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/ep/original/DT1025.jpg |

The Met’s credit line for this woodblock drawing is “Bequest of Sam A. Lewisohn, 1951,” which directly references the work that incorporates the book’s title (“Noa Noa”) in its artistic context (the painting depicts a Tahitian scene titled *Ia Orana Maria*, echoing Gauguin’s original concept)."}]

