        "armsInterventionsModule": {
          "armGroups": [
            {
              "label": "MDCO without STI",
              "type": "ACTIVE_COMPARATOR",
              "description": "1. For patients with preoperative gastrocnemius-soleus complex tightness, defined as a preoperative dorsal extension of the ankle less than 5 degrees, with the knee completely extended, a Strayer´s procedure will be performed before the other procedures.\n2. MDCO will be performed where the distal aspect of the calcaneus is separated from the proximal aspects, slided medially and fixed with two screws.\n3. After the MDCO, FDL will be transferred to the navicular bone.\n4. The spring ligament will be assessed. If ruptured, it will be reconstructed. If not ruptured, it will be tightened.\n5. A plantarflexing open wedge osteotomy of the medial cuneiform (Cotton osteotomy) will be performed if pre-/perioperative findings indicate it.",
              "interventionNames": [
                "Procedure: Conventional surgery"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "MDCO with STI",
              "type": "EXPERIMENTAL",
              "description": "1. In patients with preoperative gastrocnemius-soleus complex tightness, defined as a preoperative dorsal extension of the ankle less than 5 degrees, with the knee completely extended, a Strayer´s procedure will be performed before the other procedures.\n2. Thereafter, an STI (ProStop® Arthroereisis Subtalar Implant, Arthrex GmbH, Munich, Germany) will be inserted into the sinus tarsi.\n3. MDCO will be performed where the distal aspect of the calcaneus is separated from the proximal aspects, slided medially and fixed with two screws.\n4. After the MDCO, FDL will be transferred to the navicular bone.\n5. The spring ligament will be assessed. If ruptured, it will be reconstructed. If not ruptured, it will be tightened.\n6. A plantarflexing open wedge osteotomy of the medial cuneiform (Cotton osteotomy) will be performed if pre-/perioperative findings indicate it.",
              "interventionNames": [
